{
  "_comment": [
    "Protocol agreement vectors for the Tanaqul permissioned ledger.",
    "Two INDEPENDENT implementations must produce these byte-for-byte: the",
    "validator node's, and the platform's. Neither imports the other — the whole",
    "point of a second implementation here is that a bug in one cannot verify",
    "itself — so this file is the only thing connecting them, and both CI suites",
    "run it.",
    "WHAT THIS FILE IS NOT: proof that the values are CORRECT. It proves the two",
    "sides AGREE. Correctness is pinned separately on each side by tests written",
    "from the documented rules (the empty root is sha256 of the word 'empty', not",
    "of an empty string; merkle pairs concatenate hex TEXT, not decoded bytes;",
    "hash_timestamp is used verbatim). Agreement without those would just pin two",
    "copies of the same mistake.",
    "Field values are deliberately synthetic. These vectors exercise the FORMAT.",
    "PROVENANCE: the outputs were produced by the validator node's implementation and",
    "then verified against the platform's before being committed. Which side a vector",
    "was born from matters: it is why AGREEMENT alone is not enough, and why each side",
    "keeps correctness tests written from the documented rules."
  ],
